-- title:
--   Equal branch values at degenerate supersingular nodes
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $A$ a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (the Lean `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`), $k$ a field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism. Let $a \in k$ satisfy: $a \in$ `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no point $P$ with $q \cdot P = 0$ other than $0$; $a^{q^{2}} = a$; and the negation of the conjunction $5 \le q$, $a \ne 0$, $a \ne 1728$. Let $f$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, of the full modular function field of level $1 \cdot q$. Assume: $f$, viewed as a Laurent series, is integral over the subring `NodeLocalized.modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A.toSubring red a (a ^ q)`, consisting of those Laurent series $g$ for which $g \cdot \mathrm{modularEval}(s) = \mathrm{modularEval}(r)$ for some two-variable polynomials $r, s$ over $A$ with $\mathrm{pointEval}\,\mathrm{red}\,a\,(a^{q})\,s \ne 0$; $f$ lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the subring generated by the constant series from $A$ together with `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of level $1 \cdot q$ at the complement of the prime kernel of reduction, and its image under `modularRedLocHom` lies in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the subfield of Laurent series over $k$ generated over $k$ by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`; and the same two conditions for the image of $f$ under `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)`, the base change of the Fricke automorphism of level $1 \cdot q$. Then there is $c \in k$ such that, for each of the two places in `frobNodePair q a` — those attached to the points $a$ and $a^{q}$ respectively — the corresponding reduced function lies in the place's valuation subring and its residue is the image of $c$ in the residue field; that is, both reductions take the common value $c$ on the two branches.
--
--   This is the one-point statement at a supersingular node of the modular curve of level $q$ in the degenerate cases, where either $q < 5$ or the supersingular $j$-invariant is $0$ or $1728$, so that the node has extra automorphisms and the local equation is $uv = \varpi^{e}$ with $e > 1$. It feeds, together with the generic case, into [`ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_isIntegral_modularLocalizedAtPoint_of_pow_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_isIntegral_modularLocalizedAtPoint_of_pow_eq), which removes the case distinction.
